{"repositoryId":1413479214,"availability":"available","full":"kanisakhpara-devs/Opia-for-Windows","name":"Opia-for-Windows","description":"A local-first photo, music, and multimedia organizer, creator, and editor.","category":"Developer tools","language":"JavaScript","stars":0,"forks":0,"created":"2026-10-10T17:32:48Z","updated":"2026-10-19T06:13:08Z","branch":"main","homepage":"https://kanisakhpara-devs.github.io/Opia-for-Windows/","topics":["music-production-studio","photo-editor"],"demo":"https://kanisakhpara-devs.github.io/Opia-for-Windows/","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T07:22:40.354Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-19T07:22:40.354Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-19T07:22:40.354Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-19T07:22:40.354Z","stars":0,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Lens · Imagine · Motion · Groove · Folio · Get started · Website · Opia for Android · Changelog","Opia for Windows is a desktop app for the things you make, in five workspaces: Lens (a photo organiser and raw-style editor), Imagine (a layered picture editor), Motion (a video editor), Groove (a music studio) and Folio (a PDF editor). You switch between them with one click. Everything runs on your own computer: no account, no uploads, no subscription. A Python engine handles the files, catalogs, colour management and exports. The interface draws every photo edit on the graphics card (WebGL 2).","Every workspace has a Beginner mode that shows the essentials in bigger controls, and an Advanced mode with every panel and tool. Opia also comes in four themes, in English and Spanish, and has trackpad-friendly controls."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/kanisakhpara-devs/Opia-for-Windows/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"96660704532696c1b166db64cb7f9ff90e25f03a944f162e8c1e954af4a75d37","extractedAt":"2026-10-19T07:22:40.467Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-19T07:22:40.467Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"t